{"text": "May 26, 2011 . - Y (\n\nSteve Conaway\nWinery\nSeaway Avenue\nAlexandria Bay N.Y. 13607\n\nDear Steve,\n\nWe have met several times during my visits back tu mica way. Lou rmignt remember the\nconversation, as I arn the guy that was raised at the Holiday Motel, and as a youngster\nplayed in Capt. Mdssey\u2019s barn. My father and Captain Massey were good friends.\n\nI was very sad to read that run-off from the state\u2019s sali. pile have crept into your wells. A\nsituation all too familiar to my family. In the mid 70\u00b0s we discovered salt in our motel / _\nrestaurant well. A well that was approximately 180 feet deep and had been in place since\nthe early 50\u2019s, when my parents open our restaurant business. Prior to that time the state.\nmade no attempt to cover those salt piles.\n\nMy father approached the state about this situation and basically got nowhere for years.\nAll the state did was place a teepee type structure over the piles. From the initial\nknowledge of the salt intrusion until my father passed away in October 1981, he was\nunable to get any type of agreement / settlement. Our pipes rusted away, our ice\n\u2018machines rotted, we bought bottle water for the restaurant \u2018and we were forced to inform\nall potential motel guest that they will be taking a-salt shower.....obviously losing a\nconsiderable amount of business. Dad tried several test wells on the three-acres but\nwithout success.\n\n- [t's only my opinion, but the stress I saw my father go thru, seeing the business our\nfamily built in 1950 basically \u201cdissolve\u201d put him an early grave at 67. The thing that\nreally grips me to this day is that within a few months after my father died, the state\u2019s\nlawyers then came to my mother and wanted to make a settlement, The value was.so\ndepressed without fresh water that it was really a crime what she finally agreed to.\n\nI don\u2019t know all of the details that occurred on the property, after mom sold and moved to\nFlorida, around 1983...but I have been told that the tainted well still exist and that a\ncouple of different property owners, were not able to make a go of the business.\n\nI don\u2019t know if it will help your cause against the state but please feel free to use this\n\u2018information, NYS knowledge of salt intrusion / contamination \u201cdating back to the mid-\n70\u201d. Also, during this period I wrote letter to the.editors to all of the major news papers\nin the state. I received at least'six acknowledgements for other private property owners\nthat were experiencing the same dilemma. ;",
